\frac{x+1}{3} = \frac{2(x+1)}{6} = \frac{2x+2}{6}
\]
\[
\frac{2-3x}{2} = \frac{3(2-3x)}{6} = \frac{6-9x}{6}
\]
Now we can add these fractions together: \[
\frac{2x+2}{6} + \frac{6-9x}{6} = \frac{2x + 2 + 6 - 9x}{6} = \frac{8 - 7x}{6}
\]
The simplified expression is $\frac{8 - 7x}{6}$. </think> <answer> $\frac{8 - 7x}{6}$ </answer>

